Why your commands returned "No resources found"
kubectl get pods -l app=nginx filters pods by the label app=nginx. If that label isn't present, you get nothing back — even though the pods exist. The deployment was likely created with a different label (e.g., app=nginx-deployment, run=nginx, or similar).

